{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T20:08:50.253Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"path":"/tmp/mdocs-issue-body.md","content":"## Summary\n\nOn the Kimi Code surface, the plugin's MCP server never starts: every session start and `/reload` fails with `MCP error -32000: Connection closed`, so the `mcp__mdocs__*` tools are never available. Hooks, skills, and the SessionStart banner all work — only the MCP server spawn fails.\n\n## Root cause\n\nKimi Code spawns plugin MCP servers with the **session's project workDir as the process cwd**. The Kimi plugin manifest declares the server with a relative module path:\n\n```json\n\"mcpServers\": {\n  \"mdocs\": {\n    \"command\": \"node\",\n    \"args\": [\"./dist/mcp-server.js\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`./dist/mcp-server.js` therefore resolves to `<project>/dist/mcp-server.js` → `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` → the process exits immediately → the client reports \"Connection closed\" (-32000).\n\nHooks are unaffected because Kimi Code runs hook commands relative to the plugin root (per the surface docs), which is why PreToolUse/PostToolUse/SessionStart all function — and why the failure can look mysterious.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Chronic in the host log: `~/.kimi-code/logs/kimi-code.log` shows `mcp server unavailable server=plugin-mdocs:mdocs transport=stdio status=failed reason=\"MCP error -32000: Connection closed\"` at every session start since 2026-09-22, across multiple projects.\n- The server bundle itself is healthy: a manual stdio handshake (`initialize` → `notifications/initialized` → `tools/list`) against `dist/mcp-server.js` (harness-mdocs 2.1.0, gitSha 231a9a6) returns the full canonical 13-tool set.\n- The same command run from a project cwd dies instantly with `Error: Cannot find module '<project>/dist/mcp-server.js'` (exit 1).\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Install the plugin on Kimi Code (`/plugins install ./node_modules/harness-mdocs/src/surfaces/kimi-code/plugin`).\n2. Open any project; start a session or run `/reload`.\n3. Observe the MCP failure; `mcp__mdocs__*` tools are absent. The `mdocs` CLI fallback still works.\n\n## Workaround (local, not durable)\n\nPatch the managed manifest at `~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/kimi.plugin.json` to use an absolute path:\n\n```json\n\"args\": [\"/Users/<user>/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/dist/mcp-server.js\"]\n```\n\nConfirmed to fix the spawn. **Caveat:** any plugin reinstall/update overwrites this patch.\n\n## Suggested fixes (upstream)\n\n- Best: check whether Kimi Code's `mcpServers` entries support a `cwd` key; if so, ship `\"cwd\": \"<plugin root>\"` in the manifest.\n- Otherwise: rewrite the `args` path to absolute at install time (the installer knows the managed plugin location).\n- Alternative: ship a thin shim (shell/node wrapper in the plugin root) that resolves the bundle relative to its own location, and point the manifest at the shim.\n\n## Affected file\n\n`src/surfaces/kimi-code/plugin/kimi.plugin.json` (and the install/packaging flow that places it).\n"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T20:08:50.257Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"path":"/tmp/mdocs-issue-body.md","content":"## Summary\n\nOn the Kimi Code surface, the plugin's MCP server never starts: every session start and `/reload` fails with `MCP error -32000: Connection closed`, so the `mcp__mdocs__*` tools are never available. Hooks, skills, and the SessionStart banner all work — only the MCP server spawn fails.\n\n## Root cause\n\nKimi Code spawns plugin MCP servers with the **session's project workDir as the process cwd**. The Kimi plugin manifest declares the server with a relative module path:\n\n```json\n\"mcpServers\": {\n  \"mdocs\": {\n    \"command\": \"node\",\n    \"args\": [\"./dist/mcp-server.js\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`./dist/mcp-server.js` therefore resolves to `<project>/dist/mcp-server.js` → `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` → the process exits immediately → the client reports \"Connection closed\" (-32000).\n\nHooks are unaffected because Kimi Code runs hook commands relative to the plugin root (per the surface docs), which is why PreToolUse/PostToolUse/SessionStart all function — and why the failure can look mysterious.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Chronic in the host log: `~/.kimi-code/logs/kimi-code.log` shows `mcp server unavailable server=plugin-mdocs:mdocs transport=stdio status=failed reason=\"MCP error -32000: Connection closed\"` at every session start since 2026-09-22, across multiple projects.\n- The server bundle itself is healthy: a manual stdio handshake (`initialize` → `notifications/initialized` → `tools/list`) against `dist/mcp-server.js` (harness-mdocs 2.1.0, gitSha 231a9a6) returns the full canonical 13-tool set.\n- The same command run from a project cwd dies instantly with `Error: Cannot find module '<project>/dist/mcp-server.js'` (exit 1).\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Install the plugin on Kimi Code (`/plugins install ./node_modules/harness-mdocs/src/surfaces/kimi-code/plugin`).\n2. Open any project; start a session or run `/reload`.\n3. Observe the MCP failure; `mcp__mdocs__*` tools are absent. The `mdocs` CLI fallback still works.\n\n## Workaround (local, not durable)\n\nPatch the managed manifest at `~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/kimi.plugin.json` to use an absolute path:\n\n```json\n\"args\": [\"/Users/<user>/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/dist/mcp-server.js\"]\n```\n\nConfirmed to fix the spawn. **Caveat:** any plugin reinstall/update overwrites this patch.\n\n## Suggested fixes (upstream)\n\n- Best: check whether Kimi Code's `mcpServers` entries support a `cwd` key; if so, ship `\"cwd\": \"<plugin root>\"` in the manifest.\n- Otherwise: rewrite the `args` path to absolute at install time (the installer knows the managed plugin location).\n- Alternative: ship a thin shim (shell/node wrapper in the plugin root) that resolves the bundle relative to its own location, and point the manifest at the shim.\n\n## Affected file\n\n`src/surfaces/kimi-code/plugin/kimi.plugin.json` (and the install/packaging flow that places it).\n"}}}
