{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T20:27:44.075Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"first-project-run","step":"VERIFY","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"{\n  \"category\": \"setup\",\n  \"id\": \"mdk-first-run-gotchas\",\n  \"title\": \"MDK First-Run Gotchas\",\n  \"content\": \"## gradlew loses its execute bit\\n\\nExtracting the MDK zip (or copying the template folder) drops the execute permission on `gradlew`. Eclipse Buildship is unaffected — it invokes the wrapper differently — but CLI runs fail with `./gradlew: Permission denied`. Fix: `chmod +x gradlew`.\\n\\n## Let Eclipse sync warm the cache\\n\\nImporting the project via Buildship (Gradle sync) downloads Gradle, Minecraft, NeoForge, and the Parchment mappings. A later CLI `./gradlew runClient` then boots in minutes. Avoid running an Eclipse sync and a CLI build at the same time — they contend on `.gradle/` locks and the shared dependency cache.\\n\\n## Expected WARN lines on the first client run\\n\\nThe stock MDK example content ships no model or texture files, so the log shows `missing model for variant: 'siasworkshop:example_block#'` and `Unable to load model: 'siasworkshop:item/example_item'` (FileNotFoundException). These are WARN-level and expected — the block and item still register, appear in their creative tabs, and place fine; they only render with the missing-texture checkerboard until models are added under `src/main/resources/assets/siasworkshop/`.\\n\\n## Local tooling note: mdocs Kimi plugin patch\\n\\nThe managed Kimi plugin manifest (`~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/kimi.plugin.json`) is locally patched to launch the MCP server via an absolute path, working around a spawn-cwd bug. Reinstalling or updating the plugin reverts the patch — the upstream fix is tracked at bbaaxx/harness-mdocs#10. Symptom if reverted: `MCP server \\\"plugin-mdocs:mdocs\\\" failed: MCP error -32000: Connection closed`. The `mdocs` CLI fallback keeps working regardless (`./node_modules/.bin/mdocs`).\",\n  \"tags\": [\"mdk\", \"neoforge\", \"setup\", \"eclipse\", \"gradle\", \"tooling\"],\n  \"lifecycle\": \"stable\",\n  \"knowledge_type\": \"how-to\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"relatedInitiatives\": [\"first-project-run\"],\n  \"sourceInitiatives\": [\"first-project-run\"]\n}\n","path":"/tmp/wiki-mdk-gotchas.json"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T20:27:44.079Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"first-project-run","step":"VERIFY","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"{\n  \"category\": \"setup\",\n  \"id\": \"mdk-first-run-gotchas\",\n  \"title\": \"MDK First-Run Gotchas\",\n  \"content\": \"## gradlew loses its execute bit\\n\\nExtracting the MDK zip (or copying the template folder) drops the execute permission on `gradlew`. Eclipse Buildship is unaffected — it invokes the wrapper differently — but CLI runs fail with `./gradlew: Permission denied`. Fix: `chmod +x gradlew`.\\n\\n## Let Eclipse sync warm the cache\\n\\nImporting the project via Buildship (Gradle sync) downloads Gradle, Minecraft, NeoForge, and the Parchment mappings. A later CLI `./gradlew runClient` then boots in minutes. Avoid running an Eclipse sync and a CLI build at the same time — they contend on `.gradle/` locks and the shared dependency cache.\\n\\n## Expected WARN lines on the first client run\\n\\nThe stock MDK example content ships no model or texture files, so the log shows `missing model for variant: 'siasworkshop:example_block#'` and `Unable to load model: 'siasworkshop:item/example_item'` (FileNotFoundException). These are WARN-level and expected — the block and item still register, appear in their creative tabs, and place fine; they only render with the missing-texture checkerboard until models are added under `src/main/resources/assets/siasworkshop/`.\\n\\n## Local tooling note: mdocs Kimi plugin patch\\n\\nThe managed Kimi plugin manifest (`~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/kimi.plugin.json`) is locally patched to launch the MCP server via an absolute path, working around a spawn-cwd bug. Reinstalling or updating the plugin reverts the patch — the upstream fix is tracked at bbaaxx/harness-mdocs#10. Symptom if reverted: `MCP server \\\"plugin-mdocs:mdocs\\\" failed: MCP error -32000: Connection closed`. The `mdocs` CLI fallback keeps working regardless (`./node_modules/.bin/mdocs`).\",\n  \"tags\": [\"mdk\", \"neoforge\", \"setup\", \"eclipse\", \"gradle\", \"tooling\"],\n  \"lifecycle\": \"stable\",\n  \"knowledge_type\": \"how-to\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"relatedInitiatives\": [\"first-project-run\"],\n  \"sourceInitiatives\": [\"first-project-run\"]\n}\n","path":"/tmp/wiki-mdk-gotchas.json"}}}
