pat` (JEI), `init/data` (datagen).\n- Layered packages: `cofh.lib` (CoFHCore: api/util/init), `cofh.core` (config, network, GUI framework, mixins), `cofh.thermal.core` + `cofh.thermal.lib` (ThermalCore: RegistrationHelper, ThermalIDs, augment rules, machine/dynamo base classes).\n- Machine recipes/tags fully JSON datagen-driven; energy = Forge Energy (FE, descends from Redstone Flux). Server configs per-world; client/common split.\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- Registration discipline: `ThermalCore/src/main/java/cofh/thermal/core/util/RegistrationHelper.java`, consumed by `ThermalExpansion/src/main/java/cofh/thermal/expansion/init/registries/TExpBlocks.java`.\n- Augment (machine-upgrade) system: `ThermalCore/src/main/java/cofh/thermal/lib/util/ThermalAugmentRules.java` and `BlockItemAugmentable`.\n- Tiered machine/dynamo block-entity bases: `cofh/thermal/lib/common/block/entity` (e.g. `MachineBlockEntity`).\n- Per-expansion `compat/` + `init/data` package split; centralized changelogs in the `CoFH/Version` repo.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- Copying is legally throttled (see License); renaming variables counts as copying.\n- Legacy trap: default branches are 1.20.x — Java 17, NeoGradle (not ModDevGradle), pre-1.21 capability/networking APIs.\n- Heavy indirection across four layers; cross-repo version ranges (`cofh_core [11.0.2,11.1.0)`) make partial upgrades brittle.\n- README is license-only; official wiki/docs are stale (1.12-era).\n\n## Key links\n- https://github.com/CoFH (org)\n- https://github.com/CoFH/CoFHCore and https://github.com/CoFH/ThermalCore\n- https://github.com/CoFH/ThermalExpansion\n- https://teamcofh.com/downloads/\n- https://maven.covers1624.net/ (`com.teamcofh:cofh_core`, `thermal_core`)\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/thermal-foundation\n","path":"/tmp/page-thermal-series.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.862Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- GeckoLib is the de-facto animation/entity-model library for modded Minecraft: keyframe-based 3D animations, 30+ easings, concurrent animation stacking, sound/particle/event keyframes, math-based animations.\n- Models/animations are data-driven JSON (Blockbench \"GeckoLib\" plugin exports `.geo.json` / `.animation.json` into `assets/<modid>/{geo,animations,textures}`).\n- One codebase ships for Forge, Fabric, Quilt, and NeoForge from a multi-loader repo.\n\n## NeoForge 1.21.1 support\n- Fully supported and actively maintained. Branch `1.21.1` (updated Sep 2026) is GeckoLib 4.x — `gradle/libs.versions.toml` pins `geckolib=4.9.3`, `minecraft=1.21.1`, `neoforge=21.1.234` (range `[21.1.150,)`), Parchment `2024.11.17`, Java 21 — same MDG 2.x + Parchment toolchain as siasworkshop (its NeoForge 21.1.256 is in-range).\n- Code is directly borrowable from this branch. Do NOT use `main`: that is GeckoLib 5 (`com.geckolib`, new group/package) targeting MC 26.x-era versions.\n- Other live branches: 1.20.1, 1.21.3–1.21.11, 26.1/26.2. Modrinth lists 1.21.1 for neoforge/forge/fabric; client required, server optional.\n\n## License\n- MIT (declared in `gradle.properties` `modLicense=MIT` and on Modrinth). Note: no LICENSE file at repo root on the 1.21.1 branch — the declaration is in build metadata only.\n\n## Core API in a nutshell\nAll under `software.bernie.geckolib` in `common/src/main/java/software/bernie/geckolib/`:\n- `animatable/` — implement `GeoAnimatable`, or subtypes `GeoEntity`, `GeoItem`, `GeoBlockEntity`, `GeoReplacedEntity`; `SingletonGeoAnimatable` for server-driven sync.\n- `animation/` — `AnimationController` state machines, `AnimationState` per-frame context, `RawAnimation` builders, `EasingType`.\n- `model/` — `GeoModel` subclass pointing at your JSON assets.\n- `renderer/` — `GeoEntityRenderer`, `GeoItemRenderer`, `GeoArmorRenderer`, `GeoBlockRenderer`, `GeoReplacedEntityRenderer`, plus `layer/` render layers.\n- `cache/` + `loading/` + `resource/` — JSON model/animation loading and reload listeners; `network/` — sync packets; `service/` — platform abstraction.\n\n## Adding it as a dependency\n- Maven: `https://maven.geckolib.com` (Cloudsmith: `https://dl.cloudsmith.io/public/geckolib3/geckolib/maven/`).\n- Coordinate: `software.bernie.geckolib:geckolib-neoforge-1.21.1:4.9.3` (per `neoforge/build.gradle.kts` archive name + version catalog). Plain jar dependency under ModDevGradle.\n\n## Who uses it / practices worth borrowing\n- Used by Mowzie's Mobs, Ars Nouveau, Creeper Overhaul, ChaosAwakens, many more (wiki keeps a \"Geckolib Powered Mods\" list).\n- Multi-loader `common/` + `neoforge/` module split sharing one `accesstransformer.cfg` (`common/src/main/resources/META-INF/accesstransformer.cfg`).\n- Convention plugins + version catalog in `buildSrc/` and `gradle/libs.versions.toml`.\n- Data-driven asset pipeline decoupled from code (`loading/`, `cache/`, `resource/`).\n- `SingletonGeoAnimatable` + `network/` pattern for animation state sync without entity data params.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- Package/group fork: 4.x = `software.bernie.geckolib`, 5.x (main) = `com.geckolib` — wiki snippets may reference either.\n- 3.x→4.x API breaks; ignore pre-1.20 examples/tutorials.\n- Rendering is fully custom; check Sodium/Iris interactions before shipping fancy rendering.\n- Declared MIT but root LICENSE file absent (unverified nuance).\n\n## Key links\n- Repo: https://github.com/bernie-g/geckolib (branch: `1.21.1`)\n- Wiki: https://github.com/bernie-g/geckolib/wiki\n- Maven: https://maven.geckolib.com\n- Modrinth: https://modrinth.com/mod/geckolib\n- CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/geckolib (id 388172)\n- Discord: https://discord.gg/pPEqBgJtZW\n","path":"/tmp/page-geckolib.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.865Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Villager-overhaul mod: replaces squidward villagers with human NPCs — dialogue, relationships/marriage/children, genetics, chores, village ranks/buildings. Single-player and SMP.\n- Two codebases matter: the stale original (WildBamaBoy, MC 1.12 era) and the maintained rewrite MCA Reborn (Luke100000 et al., 2021+).\n\n## Status on MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge\n- Original (stale): `WildBamaBoy/minecraft-comes-alive`, default branch `1.12.2-6.0.1`, last push 2022-05 (final hotfix only). Forge 1.12.2, legacy MCP mappings/architectury-era tooling. Not portable directly.\n- Maintained successor — MCA Reborn: https://github.com/Luke100000/minecraft-comes-alive, default branch `1.21.1`, GPL-3.0, actively pushed (Oct 2026).\n  - 1.21.1 NeoForge build exists and is the primary release line: latest tag `8.1.7+1.21.1`; active `dev/1.21.1` branch; release channel [NeoForge 1.21.1] MCAR on CurseForge.\n  - Other branches: `1.20.1`, plus `26.1.2`/`26.2` (new calendar-versioned MC). Multi-loader: NeoForge, Fabric, Quilt.\n  - Stack verified from `gradle.properties`: MC 1.21.1, Java 21, Parchment 2024.11.17, ModDevGradle 2.0.141, NeoForge 21.1.234 — nearly identical to siasworkshop.\n\n## License\n- GPL-3.0 on both repos. Borrowing code into siasworkshop requires siasworkshop itself be GPL-3.0-compatible; linking/interaction via API is fine. Direct copy without relicensing = violation.\n\n## Architecture and repo layout\n- Original: single-module Forge 1.12.2 Gradle project, `src/main/java/mca/...` (package-per-domain: core, entity, items, network via simple channels), heavy NBT/IDataFixer style, no data-driven content.\n- Reborn (1.21.1): three-module Gradle project (`common/`, `neoforge/`, `fabric/`) — thin loader entrypoints (`neoforge/src/main/java/net/conczin/mca/neoforge/CommonNeoForge.java`) over ~490 common classes in `net.conczin.mca`:\n  - `registry/` — registration as static-map interfaces (`ItemsMCA`, `EntitiesMCA`, `SoundsMCA`, `TagsMCA`, `TradeOffersMCA`), not DeferredRegister; attributes co-registered in `EntitiesMCA.ATTRIBUTES`.\n  - `network/` — loader-agnostic payload abstraction (`Network.Registrar`/`Sender` interfaces, `HandleablePayload`, StreamCodec-based) implemented per-loader.\n  - `entity/` — `VillagerEntityMCA`, AI/relationships, plus `resources/` reload listeners loading data-driven JSON: dialogues, gifts (datapack `data/<mod>/gifts/`), names, skins, building types, tasks, rank.\n  - `client/` — custom humanoid rendering, skin catalog, GUI screens, in-game book system; mixins (`mixin/`).\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- Multi-loader `common/` + tiny `neoforge/` shim setup — copy its `settings.gradle`/`build.gradle` split.\n- Data-driven dialogue/gift/name systems: `common/.../resources/Dialogues.java`, `data/mca/dialogues/`, `data/*/gifts/`.\n- Registry idiom: `common/src/main/java/net/conczin/mca/registry/ItemsMCA.java` (map + static constants).\n- Networking abstraction: `common/src/main/java/net/conczin/mca/network/Network.java`.\n- `example/skins/` — skin/content addon pack format.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- GPL-3.0 copyleft on both; don't lift code into a non-GPL siasworkshop.\n- Original repo is 1.12-only with old mappings — inspiration only.\n- Reborn's custom registry pattern trades NeoForge conveniences (DeferredRegister, data attachments) for loader portability; Mixin-heavy client rendering.\n- CurseForge disables 3rd-party jar sharing — no Curse Maven for dev deps.\n\n## Key links\n- https://github.com/WildBamaBoy/minecraft-comes-alive\n- https://github.com/Luke100000/minecraft-comes-alive (wiki incl. Porting guide)\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/minecraft-comes-alive-reborn\n- https://modrinth.com/mod/minecraft-comes-alive-reborn\n- https://github.com/Luke100000/minecraft-comes-alive/wiki\n","path":"/tmp/page-mca.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.869Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Villager-overhaul mod: replaces squidward villagers with human NPCs — dialogue, relationships/marriage/children, genetics, chores, village ranks/buildings. Single-player and SMP.\n- Two codebases matter: the stale original (WildBamaBoy, MC 1.12 era) and the maintained rewrite MCA Reborn (Luke100000 et al., 2021+).\n\n## Status on MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge\n- Original (stale): `WildBamaBoy/minecraft-comes-alive`, default branch `1.12.2-6.0.1`, last push 2022-05 (final hotfix only). Forge 1.12.2, legacy MCP mappings/architectury-era tooling. Not portable directly.\n- Maintained successor — MCA Reborn: https://github.com/Luke100000/minecraft-comes-alive, default branch `1.21.1`, GPL-3.0, actively pushed (Oct 2026).\n  - 1.21.1 NeoForge build exists and is the primary release line: latest tag `8.1.7+1.21.1`; active `dev/1.21.1` branch; release channel [NeoForge 1.21.1] MCAR on CurseForge.\n  - Other branches: `1.20.1`, plus `26.1.2`/`26.2` (new calendar-versioned MC). Multi-loader: NeoForge, Fabric, Quilt.\n  - Stack verified from `gradle.properties`: MC 1.21.1, Java 21, Parchment 2024.11.17, ModDevGradle 2.0.141, NeoForge 21.1.234 — nearly identical to siasworkshop.\n\n## License\n- GPL-3.0 on both repos. Borrowing code into siasworkshop requires siasworkshop itself be GPL-3.0-compatible; linking/interaction via API is fine. Direct copy without relicensing = violation.\n\n## Architecture and repo layout\n- Original: single-module Forge 1.12.2 Gradle project, `src/main/java/mca/...` (package-per-domain: core, entity, items, network via simple channels), heavy NBT/IDataFixer style, no data-driven content.\n- Reborn (1.21.1): three-module Gradle project (`common/`, `neoforge/`, `fabric/`) — thin loader entrypoints (`neoforge/src/main/java/net/conczin/mca/neoforge/CommonNeoForge.java`) over ~490 common classes in `net.conczin.mca`:\n  - `registry/` — registration as static-map interfaces (`ItemsMCA`, `EntitiesMCA`, `SoundsMCA`, `TagsMCA`, `TradeOffersMCA`), not DeferredRegister; attributes co-registered in `EntitiesMCA.ATTRIBUTES`.\n  - `network/` — loader-agnostic payload abstraction (`Network.Registrar`/`Sender` interfaces, `HandleablePayload`, StreamCodec-based) implemented per-loader.\n  - `entity/` — `VillagerEntityMCA`, AI/relationships, plus `resources/` reload listeners loading data-driven JSON: dialogues, gifts (datapack `data/<mod>/gifts/`), names, skins, building types, tasks, rank.\n  - `client/` — custom humanoid rendering, skin catalog, GUI screens, in-game book system; mixins (`mixin/`).\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- Multi-loader `common/` + tiny `neoforge/` shim setup — copy its `settings.gradle`/`build.gradle` split.\n- Data-driven dialogue/gift/name systems: `common/.../resources/Dialogues.java`, `data/mca/dialogues/`, `data/*/gifts/`.\n- Registry idiom: `common/src/main/java/net/conczin/mca/registry/ItemsMCA.java` (map + static constants).\n- Networking abstraction: `common/src/main/java/net/conczin/mca/network/Network.java`.\n- `example/skins/` — skin/content addon pack format.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- GPL-3.0 copyleft on both; don't lift code into a non-GPL siasworkshop.\n- Original repo is 1.12-only with old mappings — inspiration only.\n- Reborn's custom registry pattern trades NeoForge conveniences (DeferredRegister, data attachments) for loader portability; Mixin-heavy client rendering.\n- CurseForge disables 3rd-party jar sharing — no Curse Maven for dev deps.\n\n## Key links\n- https://github.com/WildBamaBoy/minecraft-comes-alive\n- https://github.com/Luke100000/minecraft-comes-alive (wiki incl. Porting guide)\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/minecraft-comes-alive-reborn\n- https://modrinth.com/mod/minecraft-comes-alive-reborn\n- https://github.com/Luke100000/minecraft-comes-alive/wiki\n","path":"/tmp/page-mca.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.869Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Pam's HarvestCraft (MatrexsVigil / Pamela Collins): classic farming/cooking mega-mod — 80+ crops, fruit trees, gardens, bees/fish, hundreds of foods with tool-based recipes. Final HC1 repo targets MC 1.12.2, Forge 14.23.5.2768, ForgeGradle 2.3, MCP snapshot mappings, Java 8 (from `build.gradle` in repo).\n- Successor: Pam's HarvestCraft 2 (CurseForge user `pamharvestcraft`) — a reboot split into four modules: Food Core, Crops, Trees, Food Extended.\n\n## Status on MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge\n- Upstream `MatrexsVigil/harvestcraft`: frozen at 1.12.2, last activity ~2018–2019. No 1.21.1/NeoForge anything — inspiration only, code not directly portable.\n- Maintained successor — Pam's HarvestCraft 2: official, closed-distribution mod. NeoForge 1.21.1 builds confirmed for all modules (e.g., `pamhc2foodcore-1.21.1-1.0.4`, Aug 2025; `pamhc2foodextended-NEOFORGE-1.21.1-1.0.0`, Feb 2025). Also ships Forge builds for 1.19.2–1.20.4. No official public source repo — releases via CurseForge/Modrinth only. (`github.com/NegotiatorAdapt34/pams-harvestcraft-2` is an unofficial prebuilt-JAR mirror, not source.)\n\n## License\n- Custom All Rights Reserved (see repo \"About\" and CurseForge license text): code published \"for people to learn from and to help find bugs ONLY.\" Modpacks allowed if free and credited; selling, re-distribution, texture reuse, re-uploads prohibited without written permission. Artwork never reusable. Borrow ideas/approach — not code or assets.\n\n## Architecture and repo layout\n- Single module, package root `com.pam.harvestcraft` (`src/main/java/...`), organized by concern: `blocks/`, `item/`, `tileentities/`, `worldgen/`, `gui/`, `events/`, `config/`, `loottables/`, `proxy/` (ClientProxy/CommonProxy), `addons/`, `misc/`; entry `HarvestCraft.java`, `Reference.java`.\n- Pre-registry-refactor style: static item/block lists initialized in `HarvestCraftBlocks`/`HarvestCraftItems`-style classes, worldgen hooks via Forge events, config-driven feature toggles, JSON recipes/loot under `src/main/resources`.\n- Legacy Forge toolchain (FG 2.3, `minecraft { version = ... }` block, `deobfJar`/`reobfJar` tasks).\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- `worldgen/` — garden/bush scatter generation across biomes (the HC2 \"right-click harvest, replant stage\" crop model).\n- `tileentities/` + `gui/` — simple one-slot \"machine\" blocks (grinder, pot, skillet) as pattern for low-TE-cost food stations.\n- HC2's tool-in-recipe + tag-based generic recipes (\"any fruit/vegetable in a correctly tagged mod\") — very 1.21-datapack-friendly.\n- HC2's four-module split (core/crops/trees/extended) as a study in mod modularization.\n- `events/` + `config/` — lightweight hook layer keeping game logic out of main class.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- ARR license — no code or texture borrowing, ever, without written permission.\n- HC1 code uses 1.12-era APIs (registry events, capabilities, old worldgen) — nearly nothing ports mechanically to NeoForge 1.21.1.\n- HC2 has no public source; only decompiled JARs exist (license forbids non-educational decompile).\n- HC2 requires the four modules in specific combinations (Food Extended needs Crops + Trees).\n\n## Key links\n- https://github.com/MatrexsVigil/harvestcraft (HC1, 1.12.2, ARR)\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/pams-harvestcraft-2-food-core\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/pams-harvestcraft-2-food-extended\n- https://modrinth.com/mod/pams-harvestcraft-2-food-core\n- https://ftb.fandom.com/wiki/Pam%27s_HarvestCraft\n- https://www.patreon.com/pamsmods (release changelogs, 1.21.1 builds)\n","path":"/tmp/page-harvestcraft.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.870Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Client-sided config-screen library, the de-facto standard for in-game config GUIs. Two layers: a fluent `ConfigBuilder` API for hand-built screens, and optional annotation-driven \"AutoConfig\" (`@Config`/`@ConfigEntry` classes + pluggable Gson/Jankson/TOML/YAML serializers). By shedaniel (REI author).\n\n## NeoForge 1.21.1 support\n- Fully supported, released. Branch `v15` (`gradle.properties`: `minecraft_version=1.21`, `neoforge_version=21.0.167`, `base_version=15.0`).\n- Latest 1.21.1 artifact: `me.shedaniel.cloth:cloth-config-neoforge:15.0.140` (maven.shedaniel.me; Modrinth file `15.0.140+neoforge` explicitly declares loaders `neoforge`, game versions `1.21`, `1.21.1`, published 2024-09-16).\n- Repo has moved on (branches v16→v26.3 for newer MC lines; v26.3 targets MC 26.3, active Sep 2026) — v15 is frozen but stable. Note `v15` branch pins NeoForge 21.0.x while publishing declares 1.21.1 support; treat as fine in practice.\n\n## License\n- LGPL-3.0 (`LICENSE.md`, verified). Using it as a linked dependency imposes no copyleft on your mod; copying its source into siasworkshop brings LGPL obligations for that code.\n\n## Core API in a nutshell\n- Entry point: `me.shedaniel.clothconfig2.api.ConfigBuilder.create()` → `setParentScreen`/`setTitle` → `getOrCreateCategory` → `entryBuilder().startIntSlider/startBooleanToggle/startColorField/...` → `build()` returns a `Screen`; `setSavingRunnable` persists.\n- Key types: `common/.../api/ConfigBuilder.java`, `ConfigEntryBuilder.java`, `AbstractConfigListEntry.java`, `Requirement.java`; screens in `gui/ClothConfigScreen.java`, `GlobalizedClothConfigScreen.java`; ~25 ready entries in `gui/entries/` (sliders, dropdowns, keycodes, color picker, nested/subcategory lists).\n- AutoConfig: `common/.../autoconfig/` — `AutoConfig.java`, `serializer/`, `gui/registry/GuiRegistry.java` for custom field providers/transformers.\n\n## Adding it as a dependency\n- Repo `https://maven.shedaniel.me/`, coordinate `me.shedaniel.cloth:cloth-config-neoforge:15.0.140`; declare as `implementation` (or `modApi` if your config API leaks Cloth types).\n\n## Who uses it / practices worth borrowing\n- Ubiquitous on Fabric, common on NeoForge; study it as the ecosystem reference.\n- Fluent builder design: `api/ConfigEntryBuilder.java` + `impl/builders/*Builder.java`.\n- Entry (data/error state) vs widget (rendering/scroll) split: `gui/entries/` vs `gui/widget/DynamicSmoothScrollingEntryListWidget.java`.\n- Annotation-config + serializer abstraction in `autoconfig/` — good model if siasworkshop wants data-driven config.\n- Near-zero loader code: `neoforge/` holds only a demo + `UtilsImpl` — everything lives in `common` (`settings.gradle` includes common/fabric/forge/neoforge).\n- Usage examples as demo classes: `ClothConfigDemo.java`, `ClothConfigForgeDemo.java`.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- GitBook wiki is stale (covers <= v11 / 1.20.x); README points to the GitHub wiki. Default branch is `v8` (MC 1.19.1) — always read the branch matching your MC version (`v15`).\n- Client-only: no networking or server config sync; roll your own if needed.\n- Its build is Architectury Loom + Architectury plugin, not ModDevGradle — borrow architecture, not build scripts.\n- No automatic screen registration on NeoForge (no ModMenu equivalent): you must open the built screen from your own keybind/button.\n- Shadows/relocates jankson, toml4j, snakeyaml — serializer deps are self-contained.\n\n## Key links\n- https://github.com/shedaniel/cloth-config (branch `v15` for 1.21.1)\n- https://shedaniel.gitbook.io/cloth-config (docs, stale)\n- https://maven.shedaniel.me/me/shedaniel/cloth/cloth-config-neoforge/\n- https://modrinth.com/mod/cloth-config\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/cloth-config-forge\n","path":"/tmp/page-cloth-config.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.870Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\nBotania — Vazkii's flagship \"natural magic tech\" mod (magic flowers, Mana, automation without pipes/GUIs/numbers). Actively maintained; Patchouli-book-driven Lexica Botania; requires Patchouli + Curios (Forge/Neo) / Trinkets (Fabric).\n\n## Status on MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge\n- Latest released code is on default branch `1.20.x` (`gradle.properties`: `minecraft_version=1.20.1`, build 457). No 1.21.1 release on CurseForge/Modrinth as of 2026-10-07.\n- A 1.21.1 build exists only in progress: active branch `1.21.1-porting` (committed Oct 6, 2026). Its `gradle.properties` targets MC 1.21.1, NeoForge 21.1.229, Parchment 2024.11.17, Java 21, NeoForm — nearly the same stack as siasworkshop, so this branch is the correct reference.\n- Multi-loader: `Xplat` (common) + `Fabric` + `NeoForge` Gradle subprojects; Garden of Glass skyblock addon built from the same repo.\n\n## License\nCustom Botania License (`LICENSE.txt`, SPDX \"Other\"). Free use/share/adapt; distribution requires attribution to Vazkii + indication of alterations; non-monetary (no adf.ly/paywall); using code/assets requires your project be open source with a similar license clause; `vazkii/botania/api` is exempt from most clauses but must be used verbatim. Not OSI-approved — borrowing code infects siasworkshop's licensing; treat as inspiration-only unless compatible.\n\n## Architecture and repo layout\n- `Xplat/src/main/java/vazkii/botania/{api,common,client,data,network,mixin,xplat,test}` — all game logic in `common`, platform hooks via `xplat/XplatAbstractions.java` and `ClientXplatAbstractions.java`.\n- Registration is hand-rolled, not DeferredRegister: giant static-field holder classes (`common/block/BotaniaBlocks.java`, `common/item/BotaniaItems.java`, `common/block/block_entity/BotaniaBlockEntities.java`) bound to registries via consumer `init(...)` methods.\n- Capabilities: `common/BotaniaCapabilities.java` + `common/internal_caps/` — own Mana/capability abstraction over both loaders' attachment systems.\n- Data-driven: flower behavior via data components (`common/component/`), full datagen in `common/data/`, Lexica via Patchouli JSON.\n- Networking in `network/`; heavy mixins (`common/mixin/`, `client/`); Spotless + GitHub Actions CI.\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- Mana capability design: `common/BotaniaCapabilities.java`, `common/internal_caps/` — clean capability/attachment factoring.\n- Data-component-driven flower content: `common/block/flower/`, `common/component/`.\n- Corporea (in-world item indexing/autocrafting, no GUI): `common/integration/corporea/`, `api/block/corporea/`.\n- Comprehensive datagen package (`common/data/`) covering blocks/items/loot/tags.\n- Loader-neutral abstraction seam (`xplat/XplatAbstractions.java`) if siasworkshop ever goes multi-loader.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- License's copyleft-style clause: copying code into siasworkshop obligates open source + similar clause — study, don't lift.\n- `1.21.1-porting` is unstable/porting-in-motion; APIs will churn.\n- Xplat layering is a heavy abstraction for a NeoForge-only mod — borrow patterns, not structure.\n- Mixins: in-dev dependency needs `mixin.env.disableRefMap=true` JVM arg.\n- Own registration idiom means grepping for `DeferredRegister` finds nothing.\n\n## Key links\n- Repo: https://github.com/VazkiiMods/Botania (porting branch: /tree/1.21.1-porting)\n- License: https://github.com/VazkiiMods/Botania/blob/1.20.x/LICENSE.txt\n- Docs/Lexica web: https://botaniamod.net\n- Maven: https://maven.blamejared.com (group `vazkii.botania`)\n- Modrinth: https://modrinth.com/mod/botania\n","path":"/tmp/page-botania.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.870Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\nEnder IO — the classic tech mod rewritten for modern Minecraft: compact item/fluid/energy/redstone conduits, machines (SAG mill, alloy smelter, farming station, powered spawner, stirling/solar/soul power, vacuum chests, obelisks, vat...), capacitors, travel anchors, tools/armor. Core repo is `Team-EnderIO/EnderIO` (single monorepo); siblings: `Endergy` (addon), `Regilite` (archived reg-helper), `Website` (docs).\n\n## Status on MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge\n- Default branch is literally `1.21.1`; `libs.versions.toml` pins MC strictly `1.21.1`, NeoForge 21.1.216, Parchment 1.21 `2024.07.28`, ModDevGradle 2.0.124 — nearly identical toolchain to siasworkshop.\n- Latest 1.21.1 release: v8.2.12-beta (2026-09-07); branch `versionSeries=8.2`. README support table: 1.21.1 = 8.x, actively supported.\n- v9.0.x alphas target MC 26.1 (WIP). 1.20.1 line was 6.x — unsupported, maintenance PRs only.\n\n## License\n`LICENSE.txt` = Unlicense (public domain); README prose says CC0 1.0 — both public-domain-equivalent, minor mismatch. Bundled third-party APIs and some assets carry their own licenses; sound assets are CC BY / CC BY-NC 3.0 (NC is a pack-redistribution gotcha).\n\n## Architecture and repo layout\n- Modules: `endercore` (small core lib), `enderio` (the mod), `enderio-modded-conduits` (Mekanism/AE2/RS conduits).\n- Main packages under `enderio/src/main/java/com/enderio/enderio/`: `init/` (one DeferredRegister holder per registry: `EIOBlocks`, `EIOItems`, `EIOBlockEntities`, `EIOMenus`, `EIORecipes`, `EIOConduitTypes`, `EIODataComponents`...), `content/` (one folder per feature, e.g. `content/machines/sag_mill/` with its Block/BlockEntity/Menu/Screen), `foundation/` (shared infra: energy, fluid, inventory, menu, model, recipe, network), `api/` (public API incl. `api/conduits`: `Conduit`, `ConduitType`, capability accessors), `client/`, `compat/`, `mixin/`.\n- Conduit types/data/connection/node/network-context are all NeoForge registries; networks run on GraphLib3 (gigaherz), mirrored on their maven. Conduit hosting: `content/conduits/bundle/ConduitBundleBlock`.\n- Networking: custom-payload packets + client/server handlers in `foundation/network/` (`EIONetwork`, `menu_sync/` for container syncing).\n- Dedicated `datagen` and `gametest` sourceSets; generated resources committed under `src/generated/resources`. Athena CTM for connected textures.\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- `enderio/.../init/` — clean one-class-per-registry DeferredRegister pattern.\n- `content/<feature>/` co-location of every class a feature needs (great template for siasworkshop features).\n- `foundation/network/` packet/handler split plus `menu_sync` container-data syncing.\n- `api/conduits/` registry-driven conduit-type design + `ConduitBundleBlock` multi-part hosting.\n- `gradle/libs.versions.toml` with `strictly` version pins; datagen as a separate sourceSet.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- README dev snippet still shows `fg.deobf` (ForgeGradle leftover — stale; it's MDG now).\n- Regilite is archived; the 1.21.1 branch uses plain DeferredRegister — old tutorials referencing Regilite mislead.\n- Heavy `EIO*` abstraction layer and committed datagen output make casual copy-paste noisy.\n- GraphLib3 comes via `maven.rover656.dev` mirror, not a standard repo.\n- 1.20.1-era (6.x) code differs radically from 8.x; only the `1.21.1` branch is a safe borrow source.\n\n## Key links\n- Repo: https://github.com/Team-EnderIO/EnderIO\n- Docs/blog: https://enderio.com/ (source: https://github.com/Team-EnderIO/Website)\n- Maven: https://maven.rover656.dev/releases (`com.enderio:enderio:<ver>` + `:api`)\n- CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/ender-io (64578)\n- Modrinth: https://modrinth.com/mod/enderio (49ZofO4f)\n- Regilite (archived, historical): https://github.com/Team-EnderIO/Regilite\n","path":"/tmp/page-enderio.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.871Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Pam's HarvestCraft (MatrexsVigil / Pamela Collins): classic farming/cooking mega-mod — 80+ crops, fruit trees, gardens, bees/fish, hundreds of foods with tool-based recipes. Final HC1 repo targets MC 1.12.2, Forge 14.23.5.2768, ForgeGradle 2.3, MCP snapshot mappings, Java 8 (from `build.gradle` in repo).\n- Successor: Pam's HarvestCraft 2 (CurseForge user `pamharvestcraft`) — a reboot split into four modules: Food Core, Crops, Trees, Food Extended.\n\n## Status on MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge\n- Upstream `MatrexsVigil/harvestcraft`: frozen at 1.12.2, last activity ~2018–2019. No 1.21.1/NeoForge anything — inspiration only, code not directly portable.\n- Maintained successor — Pam's HarvestCraft 2: official, closed-distribution mod. NeoForge 1.21.1 builds confirmed for all modules (e.g., `pamhc2foodcore-1.21.1-1.0.4`, Aug 2025; `pamhc2foodextended-NEOFORGE-1.21.1-1.0.0`, Feb 2025). Also ships Forge builds for 1.19.2–1.20.4. No official public source repo — releases via CurseForge/Modrinth only. (`github.com/NegotiatorAdapt34/pams-harvestcraft-2` is an unofficial prebuilt-JAR mirror, not source.)\n\n## License\n- Custom All Rights Reserved (see repo \"About\" and CurseForge license text): code published \"for people to learn from and to help find bugs ONLY.\" Modpacks allowed if free and credited; selling, re-distribution, texture reuse, re-uploads prohibited without written permission. Artwork never reusable. Borrow ideas/approach — not code or assets.\n\n## Architecture and repo layout\n- Single module, package root `com.pam.harvestcraft` (`src/main/java/...`), organized by concern: `blocks/`, `item/`, `tileentities/`, `worldgen/`, `gui/`, `events/`, `config/`, `loottables/`, `proxy/` (ClientProxy/CommonProxy), `addons/`, `misc/`; entry `HarvestCraft.java`, `Reference.java`.\n- Pre-registry-refactor style: static item/block lists initialized in `HarvestCraftBlocks`/`HarvestCraftItems`-style classes, worldgen hooks via Forge events, config-driven feature toggles, JSON recipes/loot under `src/main/resources`.\n- Legacy Forge toolchain (FG 2.3, `minecraft { version = ... }` block, `deobfJar`/`reobfJar` tasks).\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- `worldgen/` — garden/bush scatter generation across biomes (the HC2 \"right-click harvest, replant stage\" crop model).\n- `tileentities/` + `gui/` — simple one-slot \"machine\" blocks (grinder, pot, skillet) as pattern for low-TE-cost food stations.\n- HC2's tool-in-recipe + tag-based generic recipes (\"any fruit/vegetable in a correctly tagged mod\") — very 1.21-datapack-friendly.\n- HC2's four-module split (core/crops/trees/extended) as a study in mod modularization.\n- `events/` + `config/` — lightweight hook layer keeping game logic out of main class.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- ARR license — no code or texture borrowing, ever, without written permission.\n- HC1 code uses 1.12-era APIs (registry events, capabilities, old worldgen) — nearly nothing ports mechanically to NeoForge 1.21.1.\n- HC2 has no public source; only decompiled JARs exist (license forbids non-educational decompile).\n- HC2 requires the four modules in specific combinations (Food Extended needs Crops + Trees).\n\n## Key links\n- https://github.com/MatrexsVigil/harvestcraft (HC1, 1.12.2, ARR)\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/pams-harvestcraft-2-food-core\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/pams-harvestcraft-2-food-extended\n- https://modrinth.com/mod/pams-harvestcraft-2-food-core\n- https://ftb.fandom.com/wiki/Pam%27s_HarvestCraft\n- https://www.patreon.com/pamsmods (release changelogs, 1.21.1 builds)\n","path":"/tmp/page-harvestcraft.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.873Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Full rewrite/continuation of Big Reactors (Erogenous Beef) by RogueLogix: multiblock fission reactors, turbines, heat exchangers, radiation-free big-power gen. Requires another mod to move/use energy.\n- Companion library mods (git submodules): Phosphophyllite (multiblock API/registry framework) and Quartz (OpenGL/Vulkan rendering + GUI lib). Org overview: https://github.com/BiggerSeries/BiggerSeries\n\n## Status on MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge\n- No 1.21.x branch exists; 1.21.1 NeoForge build is absent. Latest branches: `master` = MC 1.20.4 + NeoForge 20.4.156-beta (last commit Feb 2024); `1.20.1` = Forge 47.1.0 + Parchment (last commit Nov 2024). Releases stop at 0.6.0-beta.10.x. Effectively dormant.\n- Maintained successor (same Big Reactors lineage, different codebase): Extreme Reactors (ZeroNoRyouki) — actively released, `ExtremeReactors2-1.21.1-2.4.28` on NeoForge 1.21.1 (Dec 2025), built on its ZeroCore multiblock library. CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/extreme-reactors. This is the repo to consult for 1.21.1-native multiblock code.\n\n## License\n- LGPL-2.1 (LICENSE.txt). Author's TLDR: modpacks/PRs/library use at any license fine; redistributing builds discouraged; derivatives must stay open source. Phosphophyllite/Quartz also LGPL-2.1.\n\n## Architecture and repo layout\n- Root `build.gradle` uses NeoGradle 7.0.x (`net.neoforged.gradle.userdev`), Java 17, with `Phosphophyllite` and `Quartz` as included build submodules; mods.toml version ranges injected via `ProcessResources`.\n- Package root `src/main/java/net/roguelogix/biggerreactors/`: `multiblocks/{reactor,reactor2,turbine,heatexchanger}` (each split into `blocks/`, `tiles/`, `containers/`, `client/`, `state/`, plus `ReactorMultiblockController.java` and a `simulation/` package per machine), `registries/`, `machine/`, `fluids/`, `items/`.\n- No DeferredRegister — registration goes through Phosphophyllite's annotation-driven `Registry` (`new Registry(...)` in `BiggerReactors.java`), creative tabs pulled from the library mods.\n- Data-driven behavior registries reloaded on data reload: `ReactorModeratorRegistry`, `TurbineCoilRegistry`, `FluidTransitionRegistry` (JSON-defined moderator/coil/fluid properties).\n- Custom GPU-accelerated GUI rendering via Quartz; LWJGL OpenCL/Vulkan deps on runtime classpath.\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- Phosphophyllite multiblock framework (https://github.com/BiggerSeries/Phosphophyllite): controller/assembly validation, per-tile `state` sync — best-in-class multiblock reference.\n- Data-reloadable JSON registries for block/fluid behavior (`src/main/java/net/roguelogix/biggerreactors/registries/`).\n- Splitting each multiblock machine into self-contained packages (blocks/tiles/containers/client/simulation) under one `multiblocks/` root.\n- Simulation core decoupled from Minecraft (`multiblocks/reactor/simulation/`) — pure logic, testable.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- Dead on 1.21.1 — code borrows as inspiration only; it uses NeoGradle 7 (not ModDevGradle), Java 17 (not 21), and pre-1.20.5 data component APIs.\n- Custom `Registry` + submodule libs add learning curve; annotations are nonstandard vs. DeferredRegister.\n- Author asks you not to redistribute built jars; honor the LGPL share-alike if you port code.\n- Official wiki (biggerseries.net) returned HTTP 522 — likely down (unverified whether permanent).\n- `reactor2` package is an unfinished rewrite; don't treat it as canonical.\n\n## Key links\n- Repo: https://github.com/BiggerSeries/BiggerReactors\n- Org/readme: https://github.com/BiggerSeries/BiggerSeries\n- Phosphophyllite (multiblock lib): https://github.com/BiggerSeries/Phosphophyllite\n- CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/biggerreactors\n- Successor for 1.21.1 reference: https://github.com/ZeroNoRyouki/ExtremeReactors\n","path":"/tmp/page-biggerreactors.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.877Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Full rewrite/continuation of Big Reactors (Erogenous Beef) by RogueLogix: multiblock fission reactors, turbines, heat exchangers, radiation-free big-power gen. Requires another mod to move/use energy.\n- Companion library mods (git submodules): Phosphophyllite (multiblock API/registry framework) and Quartz (OpenGL/Vulkan rendering + GUI lib). Org overview: https://github.com/BiggerSeries/BiggerSeries\n\n## Status on MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge\n- No 1.21.x branch exists; 1.21.1 NeoForge build is absent. Latest branches: `master` = MC 1.20.4 + NeoForge 20.4.156-beta (last commit Feb 2024); `1.20.1` = Forge 47.1.0 + Parchment (last commit Nov 2024). Releases stop at 0.6.0-beta.10.x. Effectively dormant.\n- Maintained successor (same Big Reactors lineage, different codebase): Extreme Reactors (ZeroNoRyouki) — actively released, `ExtremeReactors2-1.21.1-2.4.28` on NeoForge 1.21.1 (Dec 2025), built on its ZeroCore multiblock library. CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/extreme-reactors. This is the repo to consult for 1.21.1-native multiblock code.\n\n## License\n- LGPL-2.1 (LICENSE.txt). Author's TLDR: modpacks/PRs/library use at any license fine; redistributing builds discouraged; derivatives must stay open source. Phosphophyllite/Quartz also LGPL-2.1.\n\n## Architecture and repo layout\n- Root `build.gradle` uses NeoGradle 7.0.x (`net.neoforged.gradle.userdev`), Java 17, with `Phosphophyllite` and `Quartz` as included build submodules; mods.toml version ranges injected via `ProcessResources`.\n- Package root `src/main/java/net/roguelogix/biggerreactors/`: `multiblocks/{reactor,reactor2,turbine,heatexchanger}` (each split into `blocks/`, `tiles/`, `containers/`, `client/`, `state/`, plus `ReactorMultiblockController.java` and a `simulation/` package per machine), `registries/`, `machine/`, `fluids/`, `items/`.\n- No DeferredRegister — registration goes through Phosphophyllite's annotation-driven `Registry` (`new Registry(...)` in `BiggerReactors.java`), creative tabs pulled from the library mods.\n- Data-driven behavior registries reloaded on data reload: `ReactorModeratorRegistry`, `TurbineCoilRegistry`, `FluidTransitionRegistry` (JSON-defined moderator/coil/fluid properties).\n- Custom GPU-accelerated GUI rendering via Quartz; LWJGL OpenCL/Vulkan deps on runtime classpath.\n\n## Practices worth borrowing\n- Phosphophyllite multiblock framework (https://github.com/BiggerSeries/Phosphophyllite): controller/assembly validation, per-tile `state` sync — best-in-class multiblock reference.\n- Data-reloadable JSON registries for block/fluid behavior (`src/main/java/net/roguelogix/biggerreactors/registries/`).\n- Splitting each multiblock machine into self-contained packages (blocks/tiles/containers/client/simulation) under one `multiblocks/` root.\n- Simulation core decoupled from Minecraft (`multiblocks/reactor/simulation/`) — pure logic, testable.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- Dead on 1.21.1 — code borrows as inspiration only; it uses NeoGradle 7 (not ModDevGradle), Java 17 (not 21), and pre-1.20.5 data component APIs.\n- Custom `Registry` + submodule libs add learning curve; annotations are nonstandard vs. DeferredRegister.\n- Author asks you not to redistribute built jars; honor the LGPL share-alike if you port code.\n- Official wiki (biggerseries.net) returned HTTP 522 — likely down (unverified whether permanent).\n- `reactor2` package is an unfinished rewrite; don't treat it as canonical.\n\n## Key links\n- Repo: https://github.com/BiggerSeries/BiggerReactors\n- Org/readme: https://github.com/BiggerSeries/BiggerSeries\n- Phosphophyllite (multiblock lib): https://github.com/BiggerSeries/Phosphophyllite\n- CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/biggerreactors\n- Successor for 1.21.1 reference: https://github.com/ZeroNoRyouki/ExtremeReactors\n","path":"/tmp/page-biggerreactors.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.878Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Darkhax's general-purpose library mod (\"code, frameworks, and utilities for other mods\"); docs claim 42,000+ dependent projects. Powers Enchantment Descriptions, Botany Pots, Tips, Dark Utilities.\n- Not a content mod — it's infrastructure other mods compile against. PRIORITY REFERENCE for siasworkshop.\n\n## NeoForge 1.21.1 support\n- Fully supported, actively maintained. Dedicated `1.21.1` branch: `gradle.properties` pins MC 1.21.1, NeoForge 21.1.209, Java 21, Parchment 1.21/2024.07.28, version range `[1.21.1,1.22)`.\n- Latest published `bookshelf-neoforge-1.21.1` on Maven is 21.1.81 (repo metadata updated 2026-02-10).\n- Multi-loader layout: `common/`, `neoforge/`, `fabric/` subprojects. No `forge/` dir on this branch (README's Forge line is stale). Newer branches (`26.1.1`, `26.1.2`, `26.2`, `26.3`) track newer MC versions (exact mapping unverified).\n\n## License\n- LGPL-2.1 (verified from `LICENSE` + `mod_license=LGPL 2.1`). Depends-on/linking is fine; copying code into your own mod triggers attribution + share-alike on the borrowed portion.\n\n## Core API in a nutshell\nAll under `common/src/main/java/net/darkhax/bookshelf/common/api/`:\n- `registry/` — `ContentProvider` (Darkhax's DeferredRegister replacement), `RegistryReference`, `RegistrationContext`, `adapters/` wrapping loader registries.\n- `network/` — `IPacket`, `AbstractPacket`, `INetworkHandler`, `Destination`; wrapper over vanilla/NeoForge payload registration.\n- `data/` — `codecs/` (incl. `EnumStreamCodec`, map/stream helpers), `conditions/` (custom JSON conditions), `ingredient/`, `loot/`, `enchantment/`, `BookshelfTags`, `ISidedRecipeManager`.\n- `util/` — `CommandHelper`, `DataHelper`, `ExperienceHelper`, `TextHelper`, `MathsHelper`, `TickAccumulator`; `IPlatformHelper`/`IGameplayHelper`/`IRenderHelper` service interfaces.\n- Also: `block/`, `item/`, `entity/`, `menu/`, `loot/`, `commands/`, `text/`, `annotation/`.\n- Platform abstraction: `service/Services.java` (ServiceLoader) with impls in each loader module; `common/mixin/` for shared mixins.\n\n## Adding it as a dependency\n- Repo: `https://maven.blamejared.com` (`maven { url = ... }`).\n- `implementation \"net.darkhax.bookshelf:bookshelf-neoforge-1.21.1:21.1.81\"` (README example says `21.1.0`; Maven shows 21.1.81 latest). Also `bookshelf-common-1.21.1` (compileOnly) etc. for multiloader.\n\n## Who uses it / practices worth borrowing\n- Users: Enchantment Descriptions, Botany Pots, Tips, Dark Utilities, ~42k projects per docs page.\n- `registry/ContentProvider.java` — single registration entry point per mod, loader-agnostic.\n- `service/Services.java` + per-module `impl/` — SPI-based platform abstraction worth imitating for any multiloader ambitions.\n- `network/` — minimal typed-packet layer.\n- `data/codecs/`, `data/conditions/` — reusable codec/condition toolkit for data-driven JSON.\n- Build: `buildSrc` convention plugins (`multiloader-loader`), gradle.properties-driven metadata, ModDevGradle + Parchment block in `neoforge/build.gradle` (near-identical toolchain to siasworkshop), CurseGradle + Minotaur publish tasks in the same file.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- Version numbers track NeoForge (21.1.x), not semver — check Maven for latest rather than trusting the README snippet.\n- API-first design: most logic lives in loader-neutral `common`; copy-pasting a class into a NeoForge-only mod may drag `Services` indirection with it.\n- Branch-per-MC-version: always read the `1.21.1` branch; `main`/default and newer branches target other MC versions.\n- LGPL obligations if borrowing source (not just depending).\n- The `forge` artifact line in the README is stale for this branch.\n\n## Key links\n- Repo: https://github.com/Darkhax-Minecraft/Bookshelf\n- Docs: https://docs.darkhax.net/mods/bookshelf\n- Maven: https://maven.blamejared.com/net/darkhax/bookshelf/\n- Modrinth: https://modrinth.com/mod/bookshelf-lib\n- CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/bookshelf\n","path":"/tmp/page-bookshelf.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.878Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Client-sided config-screen library, the de-facto standard for in-game config GUIs. Two layers: a fluent `ConfigBuilder` API for hand-built screens, and optional annotation-driven \"AutoConfig\" (`@Config`/`@ConfigEntry` classes + pluggable Gson/Jankson/TOML/YAML serializers). By shedaniel (REI author).\n\n## NeoForge 1.21.1 support\n- Fully supported, released. Branch `v15` (`gradle.properties`: `minecraft_version=1.21`, `neoforge_version=21.0.167`, `base_version=15.0`).\n- Latest 1.21.1 artifact: `me.shedaniel.cloth:cloth-config-neoforge:15.0.140` (maven.shedaniel.me; Modrinth file `15.0.140+neoforge` explicitly declares loaders `neoforge`, game versions `1.21`, `1.21.1`, published 2024-09-16).\n- Repo has moved on (branches v16→v26.3 for newer MC lines; v26.3 targets MC 26.3, active Sep 2026) — v15 is frozen but stable. Note `v15` branch pins NeoForge 21.0.x while publishing declares 1.21.1 support; treat as fine in practice.\n\n## License\n- LGPL-3.0 (`LICENSE.md`, verified). Using it as a linked dependency imposes no copyleft on your mod; copying its source into siasworkshop brings LGPL obligations for that code.\n\n## Core API in a nutshell\n- Entry point: `me.shedaniel.clothconfig2.api.ConfigBuilder.create()` → `setParentScreen`/`setTitle` → `getOrCreateCategory` → `entryBuilder().startIntSlider/startBooleanToggle/startColorField/...` → `build()` returns a `Screen`; `setSavingRunnable` persists.\n- Key types: `common/.../api/ConfigBuilder.java`, `ConfigEntryBuilder.java`, `AbstractConfigListEntry.java`, `Requirement.java`; screens in `gui/ClothConfigScreen.java`, `GlobalizedClothConfigScreen.java`; ~25 ready entries in `gui/entries/` (sliders, dropdowns, keycodes, color picker, nested/subcategory lists).\n- AutoConfig: `common/.../autoconfig/` — `AutoConfig.java`, `serializer/`, `gui/registry/GuiRegistry.java` for custom field providers/transformers.\n\n## Adding it as a dependency\n- Repo `https://maven.shedaniel.me/`, coordinate `me.shedaniel.cloth:cloth-config-neoforge:15.0.140`; declare as `implementation` (or `modApi` if your config API leaks Cloth types).\n\n## Who uses it / practices worth borrowing\n- Ubiquitous on Fabric, common on NeoForge; study it as the ecosystem reference.\n- Fluent builder design: `api/ConfigEntryBuilder.java` + `impl/builders/*Builder.java`.\n- Entry (data/error state) vs widget (rendering/scroll) split: `gui/entries/` vs `gui/widget/DynamicSmoothScrollingEntryListWidget.java`.\n- Annotation-config + serializer abstraction in `autoconfig/` — good model if siasworkshop wants data-driven config.\n- Near-zero loader code: `neoforge/` holds only a demo + `UtilsImpl` — everything lives in `common` (`settings.gradle` includes common/fabric/forge/neoforge).\n- Usage examples as demo classes: `ClothConfigDemo.java`, `ClothConfigForgeDemo.java`.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- GitBook wiki is stale (covers <= v11 / 1.20.x); README points to the GitHub wiki. Default branch is `v8` (MC 1.19.1) — always read the branch matching your MC version (`v15`).\n- Client-only: no networking or server config sync; roll your own if needed.\n- Its build is Architectury Loom + Architectury plugin, not ModDevGradle — borrow architecture, not build scripts.\n- No automatic screen registration on NeoForge (no ModMenu equivalent): you must open the built screen from your own keybind/button.\n- Shadows/relocates jankson, toml4j, snakeyaml — serializer deps are self-contained.\n\n## Key links\n- https://github.com/shedaniel/cloth-config (branch `v15` for 1.21.1)\n- https://shedaniel.gitbook.io/cloth-config (docs, stale)\n- https://maven.shedaniel.me/me/shedaniel/cloth/cloth-config-neoforge/\n- https://modrinth.com/mod/cloth-config\n- https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/cloth-config-forge\n","path":"/tmp/page-cloth-config.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.880Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- GeckoLib is the de-facto animation/entity-model library for modded Minecraft: keyframe-based 3D animations, 30+ easings, concurrent animation stacking, sound/particle/event keyframes, math-based animations.\n- Models/animations are data-driven JSON (Blockbench \"GeckoLib\" plugin exports `.geo.json` / `.animation.json` into `assets/<modid>/{geo,animations,textures}`).\n- One codebase ships for Forge, Fabric, Quilt, and NeoForge from a multi-loader repo.\n\n## NeoForge 1.21.1 support\n- Fully supported and actively maintained. Branch `1.21.1` (updated Sep 2026) is GeckoLib 4.x — `gradle/libs.versions.toml` pins `geckolib=4.9.3`, `minecraft=1.21.1`, `neoforge=21.1.234` (range `[21.1.150,)`), Parchment `2024.11.17`, Java 21 — same MDG 2.x + Parchment toolchain as siasworkshop (its NeoForge 21.1.256 is in-range).\n- Code is directly borrowable from this branch. Do NOT use `main`: that is GeckoLib 5 (`com.geckolib`, new group/package) targeting MC 26.x-era versions.\n- Other live branches: 1.20.1, 1.21.3–1.21.11, 26.1/26.2. Modrinth lists 1.21.1 for neoforge/forge/fabric; client required, server optional.\n\n## License\n- MIT (declared in `gradle.properties` `modLicense=MIT` and on Modrinth). Note: no LICENSE file at repo root on the 1.21.1 branch — the declaration is in build metadata only.\n\n## Core API in a nutshell\nAll under `software.bernie.geckolib` in `common/src/main/java/software/bernie/geckolib/`:\n- `animatable/` — implement `GeoAnimatable`, or subtypes `GeoEntity`, `GeoItem`, `GeoBlockEntity`, `GeoReplacedEntity`; `SingletonGeoAnimatable` for server-driven sync.\n- `animation/` — `AnimationController` state machines, `AnimationState` per-frame context, `RawAnimation` builders, `EasingType`.\n- `model/` — `GeoModel` subclass pointing at your JSON assets.\n- `renderer/` — `GeoEntityRenderer`, `GeoItemRenderer`, `GeoArmorRenderer`, `GeoBlockRenderer`, `GeoReplacedEntityRenderer`, plus `layer/` render layers.\n- `cache/` + `loading/` + `resource/` — JSON model/animation loading and reload listeners; `network/` — sync packets; `service/` — platform abstraction.\n\n## Adding it as a dependency\n- Maven: `https://maven.geckolib.com` (Cloudsmith: `https://dl.cloudsmith.io/public/geckolib3/geckolib/maven/`).\n- Coordinate: `software.bernie.geckolib:geckolib-neoforge-1.21.1:4.9.3` (per `neoforge/build.gradle.kts` archive name + version catalog). Plain jar dependency under ModDevGradle.\n\n## Who uses it / practices worth borrowing\n- Used by Mowzie's Mobs, Ars Nouveau, Creeper Overhaul, ChaosAwakens, many more (wiki keeps a \"Geckolib Powered Mods\" list).\n- Multi-loader `common/` + `neoforge/` module split sharing one `accesstransformer.cfg` (`common/src/main/resources/META-INF/accesstransformer.cfg`).\n- Convention plugins + version catalog in `buildSrc/` and `gradle/libs.versions.toml`.\n- Data-driven asset pipeline decoupled from code (`loading/`, `cache/`, `resource/`).\n- `SingletonGeoAnimatable` + `network/` pattern for animation state sync without entity data params.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- Package/group fork: 4.x = `software.bernie.geckolib`, 5.x (main) = `com.geckolib` — wiki snippets may reference either.\n- 3.x→4.x API breaks; ignore pre-1.20 examples/tutorials.\n- Rendering is fully custom; check Sodium/Iris interactions before shipping fancy rendering.\n- Declared MIT but root LICENSE file absent (unverified nuance).\n\n## Key links\n- Repo: https://github.com/bernie-g/geckolib (branch: `1.21.1`)\n- Wiki: https://github.com/bernie-g/geckolib/wiki\n- Maven: https://maven.geckolib.com\n- Modrinth: https://modrinth.com/mod/geckolib\n- CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/geckolib (id 388172)\n- Discord: https://discord.gg/pPEqBgJtZW\n","path":"/tmp/page-geckolib.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.883Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## What it is\n- Darkhax's general-purpose library mod (\"code, frameworks, and utilities for other mods\"); docs claim 42,000+ dependent projects. Powers Enchantment Descriptions, Botany Pots, Tips, Dark Utilities.\n- Not a content mod — it's infrastructure other mods compile against. PRIORITY REFERENCE for siasworkshop.\n\n## NeoForge 1.21.1 support\n- Fully supported, actively maintained. Dedicated `1.21.1` branch: `gradle.properties` pins MC 1.21.1, NeoForge 21.1.209, Java 21, Parchment 1.21/2024.07.28, version range `[1.21.1,1.22)`.\n- Latest published `bookshelf-neoforge-1.21.1` on Maven is 21.1.81 (repo metadata updated 2026-02-10).\n- Multi-loader layout: `common/`, `neoforge/`, `fabric/` subprojects. No `forge/` dir on this branch (README's Forge line is stale). Newer branches (`26.1.1`, `26.1.2`, `26.2`, `26.3`) track newer MC versions (exact mapping unverified).\n\n## License\n- LGPL-2.1 (verified from `LICENSE` + `mod_license=LGPL 2.1`). Depends-on/linking is fine; copying code into your own mod triggers attribution + share-alike on the borrowed portion.\n\n## Core API in a nutshell\nAll under `common/src/main/java/net/darkhax/bookshelf/common/api/`:\n- `registry/` — `ContentProvider` (Darkhax's DeferredRegister replacement), `RegistryReference`, `RegistrationContext`, `adapters/` wrapping loader registries.\n- `network/` — `IPacket`, `AbstractPacket`, `INetworkHandler`, `Destination`; wrapper over vanilla/NeoForge payload registration.\n- `data/` — `codecs/` (incl. `EnumStreamCodec`, map/stream helpers), `conditions/` (custom JSON conditions), `ingredient/`, `loot/`, `enchantment/`, `BookshelfTags`, `ISidedRecipeManager`.\n- `util/` — `CommandHelper`, `DataHelper`, `ExperienceHelper`, `TextHelper`, `MathsHelper`, `TickAccumulator`; `IPlatformHelper`/`IGameplayHelper`/`IRenderHelper` service interfaces.\n- Also: `block/`, `item/`, `entity/`, `menu/`, `loot/`, `commands/`, `text/`, `annotation/`.\n- Platform abstraction: `service/Services.java` (ServiceLoader) with impls in each loader module; `common/mixin/` for shared mixins.\n\n## Adding it as a dependency\n- Repo: `https://maven.blamejared.com` (`maven { url = ... }`).\n- `implementation \"net.darkhax.bookshelf:bookshelf-neoforge-1.21.1:21.1.81\"` (README example says `21.1.0`; Maven shows 21.1.81 latest). Also `bookshelf-common-1.21.1` (compileOnly) etc. for multiloader.\n\n## Who uses it / practices worth borrowing\n- Users: Enchantment Descriptions, Botany Pots, Tips, Dark Utilities, ~42k projects per docs page.\n- `registry/ContentProvider.java` — single registration entry point per mod, loader-agnostic.\n- `service/Services.java` + per-module `impl/` — SPI-based platform abstraction worth imitating for any multiloader ambitions.\n- `network/` — minimal typed-packet layer.\n- `data/codecs/`, `data/conditions/` — reusable codec/condition toolkit for data-driven JSON.\n- Build: `buildSrc` convention plugins (`multiloader-loader`), gradle.properties-driven metadata, ModDevGradle + Parchment block in `neoforge/build.gradle` (near-identical toolchain to siasworkshop), CurseGradle + Minotaur publish tasks in the same file.\n\n## Watch-outs\n- Version numbers track NeoForge (21.1.x), not semver — check Maven for latest rather than trusting the README snippet.\n- API-first design: most logic lives in loader-neutral `common`; copy-pasting a class into a NeoForge-only mod may drag `Services` indirection with it.\n- Branch-per-MC-version: always read the `1.21.1` branch; `main`/default and newer branches target other MC versions.\n- LGPL obligations if borrowing source (not just depending).\n- The `forge` artifact line in the README is stale for this branch.\n\n## Key links\n- Repo: https://github.com/Darkhax-Minecraft/Bookshelf\n- Docs: https://docs.darkhax.net/mods/bookshelf\n- Maven: https://maven.blamejared.com/net/darkhax/bookshelf/\n- Modrinth: https://modrinth.com/mod/bookshelf-lib\n- CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/bookshelf\n","path":"/tmp/page-bookshelf.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:43.883Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## The map at a glance\n\n| Target | Type | 1.21.1 NeoForge | License | Borrow level |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Ender IO (`1.21.1` branch) | mod | yes, default branch | Unlicense/CC0 | code + structure |\n| MCA Reborn (Luke100000) | mod | yes, default branch | GPL-3.0 | structure only |\n| Botania (`1.21.1-porting` branch) | mod | in progress | custom copyleft-ish | inspiration only |\n| GeckoLib 4.x (`1.21.1` branch) | library | yes | MIT | code + dependency |\n| Bookshelf (`1.21.1` branch) | library | yes | LGPL-2.1 | dependency preferred |\n| Cloth Config (branch `v15`) | library | yes | LGPL-3.0 | dependency |\n| CoFH Thermal series | mods | no (1.20.x only) | custom DBaJ | inspiration only |\n| BiggerReactors | mod | no (1.20.4); successor Extreme Reactors is on 1.21.1 | LGPL-2.1 | inspiration (successor: reference) |\n| HarvestCraft 1 / Pam's HC2 | mod | HC2 yes, no source | ARR | ideas only, never code/assets |\n| MCA original (WildBamaBoy) | mod | no (1.12.2) | GPL-3.0 | inspiration only |\n\n## Directly borrowable now (1.21.1-native, near-identical toolchain)\n\n- **Ender IO** — the #1 structural reference: one-DeferredRegister-class-per-registry in `init/`, per-feature folders in `content/`, `foundation/` shared infra, datagen as separate sourceSet. Toolchain matches ours almost exactly (ModDevGradle 2.x, Parchment, Java 21, NeoForge 21.1.x).\n- **MCA Reborn** — best reference for data-driven content (dialogues/gifts/names as datapack JSON) and a clean common/neoforge module split; GPL means look, don't lift.\n- **GeckoLib / Bookshelf / Cloth Config** — add as dependencies (coordinates on their pages); MIT/LGPL linking is compatible with our All Rights Reserved stance.\n\n## Inspiration only (older versions or restrictive licenses)\n\n- **CoFH Thermal** — machine/augment/energy design patterns (1.20.x, NeoGradle-era APIs, custom license).\n- **BiggerReactors + Phosphophyllite** — multiblock architecture; for 1.21.1-native multiblock code see Extreme Reactors / ZeroCore.\n- **HarvestCraft** — farming/cooking design; HC1 is 1.12.2 ARR, HC2 is closed-source. Design lessons only.\n- **Botania** — data-driven content and capability design from the `1.21.1-porting` branch; custom license forbids code lifting.\n\n## Genre alignment\n\nsiasworkshop lies along the lines of these examples: machines/energy (Ender IO, Thermal, BiggerReactors), farming/cooking (HarvestCraft), villagers/social (MCA), magic-tech flora (Botania). When implementing a feature, start from the reference page for its genre.\n\n## How to use these pages\n\nEach reference page lists concrete practices with repo-relative paths. When an agent implements a feature, open the named repo/branch and study the pointed-at classes. Respect the borrow level: `code + structure` (copy freely, keep attribution), `structure only` (imitate architecture, write your own code), `inspiration` (concepts only), `dependency` (link the artifact, don't copy source).\n","path":"/tmp/page-ecosystem-map.md"}}}
