terns (1.20.x, NeoGradle-era APIs, custom license).\n- **BiggerReactors + Phosphophyllite** — multiblock architecture; for 1.21.1-native multiblock code see Extreme Reactors / ZeroCore.\n- **HarvestCraft** — farming/cooking design; HC1 is 1.12.2 ARR, HC2 is closed-source. Design lessons only.\n- **Botania** — data-driven content and capability design from the `1.21.1-porting` branch; custom license forbids code lifting.\n\n## Genre alignment\n\nsiasworkshop lies along the lines of these examples: machines/energy (Ender IO, Thermal, BiggerReactors), farming/cooking (HarvestCraft), villagers/social (MCA), magic-tech flora (Botania). When implementing a feature, start from the reference page for its genre.\n\n## How to use these pages\n\nEach reference page lists concrete practices with repo-relative paths. When an agent implements a feature, open the named repo/branch and study the pointed-at classes. Respect the borrow level: `code + structure` (copy freely, keep attribution), `structure only` (imitate architecture, write your own code), `inspiration` (concepts only), `dependency` (link the artifact, don't copy source).\n","path":"/tmp/page-ecosystem-map.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T21:14:59.083Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"mod-ecosystem-research","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"node -e '\nconst fs = require(\"fs\");\nconst pages = [\n  [\"botania\", \"Botania\", [\"mod\",\"botania\",\"magic-tech\",\"data-driven\"]],\n  [\"thermal-series\", \"CoFH Thermal Series\", [\"mod\",\"thermal\",\"cofh\",\"machines\"]],\n  [\"biggerreactors\", \"BiggerReactors\", [\"mod\",\"biggerreactors\",\"multiblock\"]],\n  [\"enderio\", \"Ender IO\", [\"mod\",\"enderio\",\"conduits\",\"machines\"]],\n  [\"harvestcraft\", \"HarvestCraft\", [\"mod\",\"harvestcraft\",\"farming\"]],\n  [\"mca\", \"Minecraft Comes Alive (MCA)\", [\"mod\",\"mca\",\"villagers\"]],\n  [\"geckolib\", \"GeckoLib\", [\"library\",\"geckolib\",\"animation\"]],\n  [\"bookshelf\", \"Bookshelf\", [\"library\",\"bookshelf\",\"utilities\",\"priority\"]],\n  [\"cloth-config\", \"Cloth Config\", [\"library\",\"cloth-config\",\"config\"]],\n  [\"ecosystem-map\", \"Mod Ecosystem Map\", [\"ecosystem\",\"index\",\"orientation\"]]\n];\nfor (const [id, title, tags] of pages) {\n  const content = fs.readFileSync(`/tmp/page-${id}.md`, \"utf8\");\n  const payload = { category: \"reference\", id, title, content, tags, lifecycle: \"stable\", knowledge_type: \"reference\", confidence: \"high\", relatedInitiatives: [\"mod-ecosystem-research\"], sourceInitiatives: [\"mod-ecosystem-research\"] };\n  fs.writeFileSync(`/tmp/wiki-${id}.json`, JSON.stringify(payload));\n}\nconsole.log(\"10 payloads written\");\n' && for f in /tmp/wiki-*.json; do ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs command wiki.create --json \"$(cat \"$f\")\" | node -e \"let d='';process.stdin.on('data',c=>d+=c).on('end',()=>{try{const j=JSON.parse(d);console.log(j.id+': '+(j.success?'ok':'FAIL'))}catch(e){console.log('FAIL: '+d.slice(0,120))}})\"; done","timeout":120}}}
