{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:40:49.472Z","type":"tool","step":"COMPLETE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## Local tooling note: mdocs Kimi plugin patch\n\nThe managed Kimi plugin manifest (`~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/kimi.plugin.json`) is locally patched to launch the MCP server via an absolute path, working around a spawn-cwd bug. Reinstalling or updating the plugin reverts the patch — the upstream fix is tracked at bbaaxx/harness-mdocs#10. Symptom if reverted: `MCP server \"plugin-mdocs:mdocs\" failed: MCP error -32000: Connection closed`. The `mdocs` CLI fallback keeps working regardless (`./node_modules/.bin/mdocs`).\n\n## Creative tab bar paginates — missing tabs are often on page 2\n\nIn 1.21.1 the creative inventory tab bar paginates once the tab count exceeds one page (arrows + `1 / 2` indicator at the top). A custom tab placed late in the order (e.g., `withTabsBefore(CreativeModeTabs.COMBAT)`) lands on **page 2**. Symptom looks exactly like \"the mod's tab didn't register\": search finds the items, but the tab isn't visible. Before debugging registration, click the `>` arrow. Tab placement is controlled by `withTabsBefore`/`withTabsAfter` in the tab builder.\n\n## Convention: mod tab = full catalog, vanilla tabs = selective placement\n\nThe stock MDK sample splits content confusingly: the example item goes into the custom tab's `displayItems`, while the example block item is injected into vanilla Building Blocks via a `BuildCreativeModeTabContentsEvent` listener — so the block never appears next to the item. The convention this project follows (see `SiasWorkshopCreativeTabs`): list **all** of the mod's content in its own tab, and treat vanilla-tab placement as an optional, per-content decision in the `addCreative` listener.","oldString":"## Local tooling note: mdocs Kimi plugin patch\n\nThe managed Kimi plugin manifest (`~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/kimi.plugin.json`) is locally patched to launch the MCP server via an absolute path, working around a spawn-cwd bug. Reinstalling or updating the plugin reverts the patch — the upstream fix is tracked at bbaaxx/harness-mdocs#10. Symptom if reverted: `MCP server \"plugin-mdocs:mdocs\" failed: MCP error -32000: Connection closed`. The `mdocs` CLI fallback keeps working regardless (`./node_modules/.bin/mdocs`).","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/mdk-first-run-gotchas.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:40:49.477Z","type":"tool","step":"COMPLETE","details":{"toolName":"edit","args":{"newString":"## Local tooling note: mdocs Kimi plugin patch\n\nThe managed Kimi plugin manifest (`~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/kimi.plugin.json`) is locally patched to launch the MCP server via an absolute path, working around a spawn-cwd bug. Reinstalling or updating the plugin reverts the patch — the upstream fix is tracked at bbaaxx/harness-mdocs#10. Symptom if reverted: `MCP server \"plugin-mdocs:mdocs\" failed: MCP error -32000: Connection closed`. The `mdocs` CLI fallback keeps working regardless (`./node_modules/.bin/mdocs`).\n\n## Creative tab bar paginates — missing tabs are often on page 2\n\nIn 1.21.1 the creative inventory tab bar paginates once the tab count exceeds one page (arrows + `1 / 2` indicator at the top). A custom tab placed late in the order (e.g., `withTabsBefore(CreativeModeTabs.COMBAT)`) lands on **page 2**. Symptom looks exactly like \"the mod's tab didn't register\": search finds the items, but the tab isn't visible. Before debugging registration, click the `>` arrow. Tab placement is controlled by `withTabsBefore`/`withTabsAfter` in the tab builder.\n\n## Convention: mod tab = full catalog, vanilla tabs = selective placement\n\nThe stock MDK sample splits content confusingly: the example item goes into the custom tab's `displayItems`, while the example block item is injected into vanilla Building Blocks via a `BuildCreativeModeTabContentsEvent` listener — so the block never appears next to the item. The convention this project follows (see `SiasWorkshopCreativeTabs`): list **all** of the mod's content in its own tab, and treat vanilla-tab placement as an optional, per-content decision in the `addCreative` listener.","oldString":"## Local tooling note: mdocs Kimi plugin patch\n\nThe managed Kimi plugin manifest (`~/.kimi-code/plugins/managed/mdocs/kimi.plugin.json`) is locally patched to launch the MCP server via an absolute path, working around a spawn-cwd bug. Reinstalling or updating the plugin reverts the patch — the upstream fix is tracked at bbaaxx/harness-mdocs#10. Symptom if reverted: `MCP server \"plugin-mdocs:mdocs\" failed: MCP error -32000: Connection closed`. The `mdocs` CLI fallback keeps working regardless (`./node_modules/.bin/mdocs`).","path":"mdocs/wiki/setup/mdk-first-run-gotchas.md"}}}
