{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:45:29.741Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"cherry-village-worldgen","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"./node_modules/.bin/mdocs command initiative.create --json '{\"id\":\"cherry-village-worldgen\",\"title\":\"Cherry blossom villages (worldgen)\",\"objective\":\"Phase 1: make villages generate by default in cherry blossom (cherry_grove) biomes. Phase 2 (follow-up): rebuild village architecture in cherry blossom materials instead of oak. Ground the work in the vanilla 1.21.1 village pipeline (structures, structure sets, template pools, jigsaw) and extend it the idiomatic NeoForge way.\",\"plan\":[\"Create and activate initiative; advance workflow to EXECUTE\",\"Research the 1.21.1 village pipeline and NeoForge extension points (vanilla structure JSONs, jigsaw/template pools, MCA Reborn village injection as reference)\",\"Decide approach for phase 1 (cherry_grove placement) and implement it\",\"Verify in-game: cherry grove world, /locate structure, confirm a village generates correctly\",\"Record worldgen learnings to the wiki; COMPLETE phase 1 (phase 2 gets its own initiative)\"]}' | head -3 && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs resume cherry-village-worldgen >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step DISCOVER >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step CONTEXT >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step PLAN >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step EXECUTE >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs status | sed -n '1,3p'"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:45:29.744Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"cherry-village-worldgen","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"./node_modules/.bin/mdocs command initiative.create --json '{\"id\":\"cherry-village-worldgen\",\"title\":\"Cherry blossom villages (worldgen)\",\"objective\":\"Phase 1: make villages generate by default in cherry blossom (cherry_grove) biomes. Phase 2 (follow-up): rebuild village architecture in cherry blossom materials instead of oak. Ground the work in the vanilla 1.21.1 village pipeline (structures, structure sets, template pools, jigsaw) and extend it the idiomatic NeoForge way.\",\"plan\":[\"Create and activate initiative; advance workflow to EXECUTE\",\"Research the 1.21.1 village pipeline and NeoForge extension points (vanilla structure JSONs, jigsaw/template pools, MCA Reborn village injection as reference)\",\"Decide approach for phase 1 (cherry_grove placement) and implement it\",\"Verify in-game: cherry grove world, /locate structure, confirm a village generates correctly\",\"Record worldgen learnings to the wiki; COMPLETE phase 1 (phase 2 gets its own initiative)\"]}' | head -3 && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs resume cherry-village-worldgen >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step DISCOVER >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step CONTEXT >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step PLAN >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step EXECUTE >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs status | sed -n '1,3p'"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:46:01.315Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"cherry-village-worldgen","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Research village worldgen extension","prompt":"You are researching how to extend Minecraft village world generation for a NeoForge 1.21.1 mod called siasworkshop (MC 1.21.1, NeoForge 21.1.256, Java 21, ModDevGradle 2.x). \n\nCONTEXT: Vanilla villages in 1.21.1 are jigsaw structures: `worldgen/structure` registry entries (e.g. `minecraft:village_plains`) each with a `biomes` field, grouped in `worldgen/structure_set` (e.g. `minecraft:villages` with `village_plains/desert/savanna/snowy/taiga`), whose pieces come from `worldgen/template_pool` JSONs referencing NBT structure files under `data/minecraft/structures/village/...`.\n\nQUESTIONS TO ANSWER (use web: NeoForge docs at docs.neoforged.net, GitHub sources, Minecraft Wiki, MCA Reborn repo at https://github.com/Luke100000/minecraft-comes-alive — it injects custom village buildings into villages and has a wiki with porting/structure notes):\n\n1. What is the idiomatic NeoForge 1.21.1 way to make vanilla villages (or a custom village variant) spawn in ADDITIONAL biomes (specifically minecraft:cherry_grove)? Compare: (a) overriding vanilla `data/minecraft/worldgen/structure/village_*.json` from a mod's own data pack, (b) registering a custom structure/structure-set, (c) any NeoForge hooks/events for structure biome selection (e.g. structure spawns-related events, `StructureSpawnIndexGatherEvent`?? verify existence), (d) biome modifiers — confirm whether `neoforge:biome_modifiers` can affect structures or only features/carvers. Give a recommendation for the cleanest minimal approach.\n2. How exactly does a custom jigsaw structure get registered in code on 1.21.1 NeoForge (DeferredRegister for Registries.STRUCTURE etc., structure types, structure sets, spacing/separation, code vs JSON)? Is full-JSON (data-driven structure via `data/<modid>/worldgen/structure/*.json` + structure_set) possible without code? What about template pools referencing VANILLA nbt templates — any pitfalls?\n3. How does MCA Reborn (Luke100000 repo, branch 1.21.1) inject its buildings into vanilla villages? Which files/classes — look at its `common/src/main/resources/data/` and any structure-related code. Summarize the mechanism precisely (it is the team's chosen reference for village work).\n4. For the later phase (villages built from cherry wood instead of oak): what are the options — custom template pools with custom NBT structure files (how are NBT templates authored: structure block saving, programs like Axiom? can they be generated programmatically via StructureTemplateManager?), code-driven piece generation, or post-generation block replacement? What do mods actually do?\n\nOUTPUT: a tight brief (max ~500 words) with: recommended phase-1 approach with concrete file paths/registry ids, key code/registry facts for 1.21.1 (exact JSON field names, registry names), the MCA Reborn mechanism in 3-5 bullets, and phase-2 options with trade-offs. Mark anything unverifiable. Include source URLs.","run_in_background":true,"subagent_type":"explore"}}}
