{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:05:00.247Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"cherry-village-worldgen","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## The village pipeline in 1.21.1 (verified from the client jar)\n\n- Villages are `minecraft:jigsaw` structures: `data/minecraft/worldgen/structure/village_<style>.json` each declares `\"biomes\": \"#minecraft:has_structure/village_<style>\"`, `\"start_pool\": \"minecraft:village/<style>/town_centers\"`, `size: 6`, `terrain_adaptation: \"beard_thin\"`.\n- All five styles are bundled in one `data/minecraft/worldgen/structure_set/villages.json` (`random_spread`, spacing 34, separation 8, salt 10387312).\n- Pieces come from `worldgen/template_pool/village/<style>/{town_centers,streets,houses,terminators,decor,villagers,...}.json`, referencing NBT templates under `data/minecraft/structures/village/...`.\n- **Villagers spawn from the separate `village/<style>/villagers` pools** (NBTs containing villager entities) — replacing only house templates produces empty villages.\n\n## Phase 1 (done): villages in cherry groves — tag injection\n\nOne file in the mod: `src/main/resources/data/minecraft/tags/worldgen/biome/has_structure/village_plains.json`:\n\n```json\n{ \"replace\": false, \"values\": [\"minecraft:cherry_grove\"] }\n```\n\nTags merge across all data packs by path, so `cherry_grove` joins vanilla's `plains` + `meadow` in the plains-village biome tag. Plains style was chosen as the aesthetic match (meadows are cherry groves' neighbor biome). No code, no overrides.\n\nAlternatives considered and rejected (verified against neoforge-21.1.256): NeoForge `StructureModifier`s only wrap spawn overrides — cannot change structure biomes; biome modifiers cover features/carvers/spawns/climate only; a custom structure set would require overriding the vanilla `villages` set (mod-conflict-prone).\n\n## Verification recipe (deterministic)\n\n1. Create a **Single Biome** world with **Cherry Grove** (More World Options -> world type).\n2. `/locate structure minecraft:village_plains` — every chunk is cherry grove, so a hit proves the structure now qualifies for the biome. The command names the structure, so a hit IS the precise check (not just \"changes did something\").\n3. Villagers present confirm the full pipeline; they spawn from the vanilla plains `villagers` pool, unaffected by biome-tag changes.\n\n## Phase 2 (planned): cherry-material villages\n\n- Build a custom `siasworkshop:village_cherry` jigsaw structure (100% datapack JSON is possible: structure, own structure_set with own salt, template pools, processor lists) with template pools pointing at OUR NBT templates authored via structure blocks (48^3 limit per piece; link with jigsaw blocks) or Axiom.\n- References: TelepathicGrunt/StructureTutorialMod (structure datagen), ChoiceTheorem's Overhauled Village and Repurposed Structures (proven material-themed village template packs).\n- Pitfalls: match vanilla `projection` (houses/town centers `rigid`, streets/terminators `terrain_matching`); use `legacy_single_pool_element` like vanilla; remember the `villagers` pool; do NOT override vanilla pools (conflicts with other village mods); MCA Reborn is NOT a worldgen reference (its villages are runtime SavedData scanning player builds).\n","path":"/tmp/page-village-worldgen.md"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:05:00.252Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"cherry-village-worldgen","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"write","args":{"content":"## The village pipeline in 1.21.1 (verified from the client jar)\n\n- Villages are `minecraft:jigsaw` structures: `data/minecraft/worldgen/structure/village_<style>.json` each declares `\"biomes\": \"#minecraft:has_structure/village_<style>\"`, `\"start_pool\": \"minecraft:village/<style>/town_centers\"`, `size: 6`, `terrain_adaptation: \"beard_thin\"`.\n- All five styles are bundled in one `data/minecraft/worldgen/structure_set/villages.json` (`random_spread`, spacing 34, separation 8, salt 10387312).\n- Pieces come from `worldgen/template_pool/village/<style>/{town_centers,streets,houses,terminators,decor,villagers,...}.json`, referencing NBT templates under `data/minecraft/structures/village/...`.\n- **Villagers spawn from the separate `village/<style>/villagers` pools** (NBTs containing villager entities) — replacing only house templates produces empty villages.\n\n## Phase 1 (done): villages in cherry groves — tag injection\n\nOne file in the mod: `src/main/resources/data/minecraft/tags/worldgen/biome/has_structure/village_plains.json`:\n\n```json\n{ \"replace\": false, \"values\": [\"minecraft:cherry_grove\"] }\n```\n\nTags merge across all data packs by path, so `cherry_grove` joins vanilla's `plains` + `meadow` in the plains-village biome tag. Plains style was chosen as the aesthetic match (meadows are cherry groves' neighbor biome). No code, no overrides.\n\nAlternatives considered and rejected (verified against neoforge-21.1.256): NeoForge `StructureModifier`s only wrap spawn overrides — cannot change structure biomes; biome modifiers cover features/carvers/spawns/climate only; a custom structure set would require overriding the vanilla `villages` set (mod-conflict-prone).\n\n## Verification recipe (deterministic)\n\n1. Create a **Single Biome** world with **Cherry Grove** (More World Options -> world type).\n2. `/locate structure minecraft:village_plains` — every chunk is cherry grove, so a hit proves the structure now qualifies for the biome. The command names the structure, so a hit IS the precise check (not just \"changes did something\").\n3. Villagers present confirm the full pipeline; they spawn from the vanilla plains `villagers` pool, unaffected by biome-tag changes.\n\n## Phase 2 (planned): cherry-material villages\n\n- Build a custom `siasworkshop:village_cherry` jigsaw structure (100% datapack JSON is possible: structure, own structure_set with own salt, template pools, processor lists) with template pools pointing at OUR NBT templates authored via structure blocks (48^3 limit per piece; link with jigsaw blocks) or Axiom.\n- References: TelepathicGrunt/StructureTutorialMod (structure datagen), ChoiceTheorem's Overhauled Village and Repurposed Structures (proven material-themed village template packs).\n- Pitfalls: match vanilla `projection` (houses/town centers `rigid`, streets/terminators `terrain_matching`); use `legacy_single_pool_element` like vanilla; remember the `villagers` pool; do NOT override vanilla pools (conflicts with other village mods); MCA Reborn is NOT a worldgen reference (its villages are runtime SavedData scanning player builds).\n","path":"/tmp/page-village-worldgen.md"}}}
