{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:13:01.225Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"cherryfy-villages","step":"EXECUTE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"./node_modules/.bin/mdocs command initiative.create --json '{\"id\":\"cherryfy-villages\",\"title\":\"Cherry-theme all villages (cosmetic)\",\"objective\":\"Make ALL vanilla villages, in every biome, generate with cherry-blossom materials (cherry planks/logs/doors/stairs and cherry trees) instead of their native wood — a cosmetic reskin, no biome changes. Micro-biomes around villages were considered and rejected (biomes are fixed before structures generate; local biomes require replacing the worldgen pipeline, which impacts gameplay). Phase 1 (villages spawn in cherry groves) stays as-is.\",\"plan\":[\"Create and activate initiative; advance workflow to EXECUTE\",\"Implement CherryfyProcessor: state-aware oak-family (then acacia/spruce) to cherry mapping, registered as a structure processor type, plus a cherryfy processor_list JSON\",\"Override plains village template pools (houses/streets/town_centers) to attach the processor — MVP scope\",\"Add cherry trees to village decor via decor pool override (feature pool element)\",\"Verify in-game: /place structure and natural villages across biomes — materials, trees, villagers present, chests/loot intact, no broken block states\",\"Roll out to savanna, snowy, taiga (desert style: decide mapping — sandstone has no cherry equivalent, likely keep structure stone and swap wood accents only)\",\"Record learnings; COMPLETE\"]}' | head -3 && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs resume cherryfy-villages >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step DISCOVER >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step CONTEXT >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step PLAN >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs step EXECUTE >/dev/null && ./node_modules/.bin/mdocs status | sed -n '1,3p'"}}}
