{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:47:32.418Z","type":"tool","initiativeId":"multi-version-release-setup-1-20-1-1-21-1","step":"PLAN","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Port mod sources to 1.20.1","prompt":"You are working in /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/siasworkshop, a NeoForge Minecraft mod (mod id `siasworkshop`), currently on git branch `version/1.20.1`. The Gradle build has already been converted to Minecraft 1.20.1 via ModDevGradle's legacy plugin: `./gradlew compileJava` resolves and runs (takes ~3 min first time, then ~30s). Your job: port ALL Java sources under src/main/java from Minecraft 1.21.1/NeoForge 21.1 APIs to 1.20.1/NeoForge 47.1.106 APIs, iterating until `./gradlew build` passes with zero errors. Do NOT git commit anything. Do NOT touch mdocs/ or IDEAS.md.\n\nCRITICAL CONTEXT — package/distro facts for NeoForge 1.20.1 (47.1.x line, Forge-compatible):\n- Package root is `net.minecraftforge.*` (the `net.neoforged.neoforge.*` rename happened in 1.20.2+). E.g. `net.minecraftforge.registries.DeferredRegister`, `net.minecraftforge.common.ModConfigSpec`, `net.minecraftforge.fml.config.ModConfig`, `net.minecraftforge.fml.common.Mod`, `net.minecraftforge.common.MinecraftForge` (replaces `NeoForge.EVENT_BUS`), `net.minecraftforge.eventbus.api.IEventBus`.\n- Forge 47.1 has no `DeferredHolder`/`DeferredBlock`/`DeferredItem` — it uses `RegistryObject<T>`. `DeferredRegister.Blocks`/`DeferredRegister.Items` inner classes exist with `registerBlock(name, Supplier)/registerItem(name, Function, Props)/registerSimpleBlockItem`? Verify against the sources jar before assuming; fall back to plain `DeferredRegister<Block>`/`DeferredRegister<Item>` + `register(name, () -> ...)` + manual `BlockItem` registration if helpers differ.\n- No data components (1.20.5+ feature). Item stack data lives in share NBT: `stack.getOrCreateTag()`, `stack.hasTag()`, `stack.getTag()`, `tag.putLong(key, pos.asLong())`, `BlockPos.of(tag.getLong(key))`. NBT syncs to client on item stacks automatically, same role the component played.\n- Client item property: `net.minecraft.client.renderer.item.ItemProperties.register(item, ResourceLocation, ItemPropertyFunction)` — same idea, register inside FMLClientSetupEvent `enqueueWork`.\n- `CompassItemPropertyFunction` in 1.20.1: verify whether its constructor takes a `CompassTarget` functional interface (check the sources jar at build/moddev/artifacts/*sources*.jar — unzip -p ... net/minecraft/client/renderer/item/CompassItemPropertyFunction.java). If yes, keep our subclass approach (mirror trick). If the 1.20.1 variant has no pluggable target, implement `ClampedItemPropertyFunction` directly with the same math (atan2 angle, positiveModulo; wobble optional — a stable needle is acceptable for v1).\n- Block interaction: 1.20.1 has no `useWithoutItem` — override `use(BlockState, Level, BlockPos, Player, InteractionHand, BlockHitResult)` returning InteractionResult.\n- Menus: Forge 47.1 has `IMenuTypeExtension` (net.minecraftforge.common.extensions? verify) or use `IForgeMenuType.create(...)` (net.minecraftforge.common.extensions.IForgeMenuType) with `IContainerFactory` over plain `FriendlyByteBuf` (no RegistryFriendlyByteBuf in 1.20.1). Screen registration: `MenuScreens.register(MenuType, ScreenConstructor)` is PUBLIC in 1.20.1 (verify); there may be no RegisterMenuScreensEvent — use vanilla registration in client setup enqueueWork.\n- Opening the BE menu server-side: `NetworkHooks.openScreen(serverPlayer, menuProvider, buf -> buf.writeBlockPos(pos))` (net.minecraftforge.network.NetworkHooks).\n- Buttons: client `minecraft.gameMode.handleInventoryButtonClick(containerId, id)` → server `AbstractContainerMenu.clickMenuButton` — unchanged.\n- BlockEntity NBT: 1.20.1 has NO HolderLookup.Provider params — override `saveAdditional(CompoundTag)` and `load(CompoundTag)`. `tag.getString/getBoolean/getCompound` plain.\n- `net.minecraft.world.level.chunk.ChunkStatus` (no `.chunk.status` subpackage in 1.20.1).\n- Config: `ModConfigSpec.Builder` + `ConfigValue<Boolean>` (Forge 47.1: `define(name, default)` returns ConfigValue<Boolean>; `.get()` — if BooleanValue exists you may use it, but `.get()` is safe). Registration in mod constructor: `modContainer.registerConfig(ModConfig.Type.SERVER, spec)` — same.\n- Creative tab event: Forge 47.1 `net.minecraftforge.event.BuildCreativeModeTabContentsEvent` — verify name in sources.\n- `StructureManager` package in 1.20.1, `ServerLevel.findNearestMapStructure(TagKey<Structure>, BlockPos, int, boolean)`, `StructureTags.VILLAGE`, `StructureStart.placeInChunk(...)`, `Structure.generate(...)` signature, `setStartForStructure(...)` — VERIFY ALL against the 1.20.1 sources jar (build/moddev/artifacts/, look for a *sources*.jar; extract with unzip -p). These APIs moved around 1.20.2-1.20.5; trust only the 1.20.1 sources.\n- `appendHoverText(ItemStack, Level, List<Component>, TooltipFlag)` in 1.20.1 (no TooltipContext param).\n- `InteractionResult.sidedSuccess(boolean)` exists in 1.20.1.\n- `SectionPos.of(ChunkPos, int)` and `BlockPos.containing/getCenter` — verify; 1.20.1 has `SectionPos.of(ChunkPos,int)` I believe.\n- Structure processor / template pool / WoodFamily codec code is version-stable — expect few or no changes there beyond imports.\n- Entrypoint wiring class is `SiasWorkshop.java` (uses @Mod, registers DeferredRegisters); client-only class `SiasWorkshopClient.java` (@Mod dist=CLIENT). `NeoForge.EVENT_BUS.register(this)` was removed earlier; if any code still references NeoForge classes, port to MinecraftForge.\n\nDatagen (src/main/java/com/siaws/siawsmod/data/): port to 1.20.1 Forge datagen APIs (BlockStateProvider/ItemModelProvider constructors take PackOutput + ExistingFileHelper (+ mod id for item models); BlockLootSubProvider constructor and loot output dir differ — in 1.20.1 generated loot goes to `data/<modid>/loot_tables/blocks/` (plural, underscore) vs 1.21's `loot_table/blocks/`. After porting, delete stale 1.21-format generated files under src/generated/resources (loot_table/ dir) and run `./gradlew runData` to regenerate, then `./gradlew build` must be green.\n\nResources (src/main/resources): keep as-is (JSON formats for template pools, processor lists, tags, compass override model, lang are 1.20.1-compatible). One exception to verify at runtime later, not now: mods.toml dependency modId may need to be \"forge\" vs \"neoforge\" — do not change unless compile forces it; note it in your report.\n\nProcess: port file by file (all files under src/main/java), run `./gradlew compileJava`, fix errors iteratively, then `./gradlew runData` (regenerate), then `./gradlew build` green. Report back: (1) final build status, (2) list of files changed and the key API substitution per file, (3) anything you had to verify against sources and what you found (especially StructureManager/generate/placeInChunk/findNearestMapStructure/CompassItemPropertyFunction/IMenuTypeExtension), (4) any behavior deltas or things left for runtime verification (mods.toml modid, reobf, etc.), (5) confirmation you did not commit."}}}
